## Why This Is Asked

Tests for event driven checkout pipelines must prove correctness under partial failures and retries, with cross service consistency guarantees. This question probes data seeding, fault injection, idempotency, and multi-region convergence.

## Key Concepts

- Event driven end-to-end flows across microservices
- Exactly-once processing and idempotent handling
- Fault injection and chaos testing in distributed systems
- Feature flag controlled behavior and regional data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo test sketch
async function testCheckoutE2E() {
  seedRegion('us-east');
  publish('checkout', 'OrderRequested', { orderId:'ORD-1', region:'us-east' });
  enableFeatureFlag('newCheckoutFlow');
  await awaitConvergence('ORD-1', 5000);
  const ledger = readLedger('ORD-1');
  assert(ledger.status === 'COMPLETED' && ledger.total > 0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure test flakiness and stabilize seeds?
- What metrics indicate successful convergence across regions?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical E2E skills: gating UX with feature flags, deterministic tests, data seeding, and test isolation using Cypress or Playwright.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding per run
- LocalStorage state as idempotence marker
- Network/mocks to deterministically simulate flag responses
- Time-bounded execution for beginner scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
test('onboarding respects flag', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/flags**', r => r.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ onboarding: true }) }));
  await page.goto('https://app.local/');
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeVisible();
  await page.locator('#finish').click();
  const stored = await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.getItem('onboarding_complete'));
  expect(stored).toBe('true');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to multi-tenant setups with per-tenant flag overrides?
- How would you ensure the test remains reliable when the flag toggles during a session?

